abel":"B","text":"the February flooding"},{"label":"C","text":"the substrate type"}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":381.4,"text":"We think it's the shade. The upstream site has no tree cover at all, so it warms up considerably in summer."}}]},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:s3:g4","ordinal":4,"instructions":"Questions 29-30\nComplete the sentences below.\nWrite NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q29","ordinal":29,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"For temperature they have only ………, not continuous logging.","options":null,"correct_answer":"spot readings","accepted_variants":["spot"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":394.7,"text":"We have spot readings, not continuous logging."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q30","ordinal":30,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"They will send a draft by the end of ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"next week","accepted_variants":["end of next week"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":404.3,"text":"We were hoping for the end of next week, if that's not too late."}}]}]},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:s4","kind":"listening","ordinal":4,"duration_seconds":510,"stimulus":{"type":"audio","audio_url":"audio/original-listening-1.mp3","transcript":[],"markers":[{"question_ordinal":31,"time_seconds":440.6,"text":"Before the railways, every town in Britain kept its own time, set by the sun. Bristol clocks ran about ten minutes behind London, and nobody found this inconvenient."},{"question_ordinal":32,"time_seconds":452.9,"text":"What changed was not technology but scheduling. A timetable is meaningless if the two ends of the line disagree about when noon is."},{"question_ordinal":33,"time_seconds":461.8,"text":"The Great Western Railway adopted London time across its network in eighteen forty, and other companies followed within the decade."},{"question_ordinal":34,"time_seconds":470.4,"text":"For some years the two systems ran side by side. A number of town clocks were fitted with a second minute hand showing railway time."},{"question_ordinal":35,"time_seconds":479.7,"text":"Resistance was real, and it was mostly legal rather than sentimental. Court cases turned on which time a contract referred to."},{"question_ordinal":36,"time_seconds":488.9,"text":"The most cited example is a case in eighteen fifty-eight in Dorchester, where a hearing was lost because the judge used local time and the defendant arrived on railway time."},{"question_ordinal":37,"time_seconds":500.4,"text":"Parliament did not settle the matter until eighteen eighty, when Greenwich Mean Time was given legal force throughout Great Britain."},{"question_ordinal":38,"time_seconds":508.6,"text":"The international problem was harder, and it was solved by a conference in Washington in eighteen eighty-four, which chose Greenwich as the prime meridian."},{"question_ordinal":39,"time_seconds":518.2,"text":"The vote was not unanimous. France abstained, and continued to define its own time by reference to Paris for another quarter of a century."},{"question_ordinal":40,"time_seconds":528,"text":"What I want you to take from this is that standardisation is rarely a technical achievement. It is almost always a negotiation, and the winner is usually whoever already runs the network."}]},"groups":[{"external_id":"original-listening-1:s4:g1","ordinal":1,"instructions":"Questions 31-40\nComplete the sentences below.\nWrite NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q31","ordinal":31,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"Bristol clocks ran about ……… behind London.","options":null,"correct_answer":"ten minutes","accepted_variants":["10 minutes","ten"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":440.6,"text":"Before the railways, every town in Britain kept its own time, set by the sun. Bristol clocks ran about ten minutes behind London, and nobody found this inconvenient."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q32","ordinal":32,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"What forced the change was not technology but ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"scheduling","accepted_variants":["timetables"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":452.9,"text":"What changed was not technology but scheduling. A timetable is meaningless if the two ends of the line disagree about when noon is."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q33","ordinal":33,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"The Great Western Railway adopted London time in ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"1840","accepted_variants":["eighteen forty"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":461.8,"text":"The Great Western Railway adopted London time across its network in eighteen forty, and other companies followed within the decade."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q34","ordinal":34,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"Some town clocks were fitted with a second ……… showing railway time.","options":null,"correct_answer":"minute hand","accepted_variants":["second minute hand"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":470.4,"text":"For some years the two systems ran side by side. A number of town clocks were fitted with a second minute hand showing railway time."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q35","ordinal":35,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"Resistance to the change was mostly ……… rather than sentimental.","options":null,"correct_answer":"legal","accepted_variants":["law"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":479.7,"text":"Resistance was real, and it was mostly legal rather than sentimental. Court cases turned on which time a contract referred to."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q36","ordinal":36,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"The most cited court case took place in ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"Dorchester","accepted_variants":["dorchester"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":488.9,"text":"The most cited example is a case in eighteen fifty-eight in Dorchester, where a hearing was lost because the judge used local time and the defendant arrived on railway time."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q37","ordinal":37,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"Greenwich Mean Time was given legal force in ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"1880","accepted_variants":["eighteen eighty"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":500.4,"text":"Parliament did not settle the matter until eighteen eighty, when Greenwich Mean Time was given legal force throughout Great Britain."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q38","ordinal":38,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"The international conference was held in ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"Washington","accepted_variants":["washington"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":508.6,"text":"The international problem was harder, and it was solved by a conference in Washington in eighteen eighty-four, which chose Greenwich as the prime meridian."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q39","ordinal":39,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"……… abstained from the vote and kept its own time.","options":null,"correct_answer":"France","accepted_variants":["france"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":518.2,"text":"The vote was not unanimous. France abstained, and continued to define its own time by reference to Paris for another quarter of a century."}},{"external_id":"original-listening-1:q40","ordinal":40,"type":"sentence_completion","prompt":"The lecturer argues standardisation is almost always a ……….","options":null,"correct_answer":"negotiation","accepted_variants":["a negotiation"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":528,"text":"What I want you to take from this is that standardisation is rarely a technical achievement. It is almost always a negotiation, and the winner is usually whoever already runs the network."}}]}]}]}$seed$::jsonb);

select seed_test($seed${"external_id":"listening","title":"IELTS Listening Test 2","is_full_mock":false,"is_published":true,"source_provenance":{"origin":"Listening.html","watermark":"@MINDLESS_WRITER","shippable":false,"repaired_by":"content/repairs/listening.json"},"sections":[{"external_id":"listening:s1","kind":"listening","ordinal":1,"duration_seconds":510,"stimulus":{"type":"audio","audio_url":"audio/listening.mp3","transcript":[{"speaker":null,"text":"Section 1. You will hear a woman phoning a cleaning agency to arrange a regular clean."},{"speaker":"a friend of mine","text":"Good morning, Homecare Cleaning Agency. — Oh, hello. I'd like to arrange to have some cleaning done, please. — Have you used our services before? — No, I haven't, but a friend of mine has often used your company and suggested I phone you. — First of all, what area are you in? — 1I'm in the South West."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Are you interested in having a regular cleaner or is this a one-off clean? — I'd like to arrange to have someone come in once a week. — How many bedrooms does it have? — Three. — Are they all double bedrooms? — 2Well, one of the bedrooms is quite small, so it's probably really two double rooms. 3We have the small bedroom set up as an office."},{"speaker":null,"text":"And just a standard kitchen, lounge, dining room and bathroom? — Well, actually, we don't have a separate dining room. It's a kitchen-diner. 4Then there's the lounge, and as well as that, we have a family room. Oh, and two bathrooms."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Do you clean windows? — I'm afraid we don't do that, health and safety regulations, but we do offer other special services. We can put clean sheets on the beds, for example. Or we can clean out your fridge. — 5I'm not so worried about that, but I would like the sheets changed. — That's no problem. We can do that (A) (windows — rad etildi, fridge — rad etildi)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"What about the carpet? As well as the standard vacuum, we can shampoo it if you want. — We've got young children, so it gets pretty dirty. I haven't had it done for six months. — 6It really needs doing more often than that. You can have it done every month if you like, but three months is what we usually recommend (B — the carpet)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Do you do laundry work? What exactly would you like done? — 7Well, it's no problem to put a load of washing in the machine. I can do that, but I would like to have the ironing done (B). — And would you like the washing put away in drawers or wardrobes? — No, it's okay. You can just leave everything out (A va C — rad etildi)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"What's your full name? — It's Rose Kelly. — And could I have your home address? — 8Yes. It's 48 Ames Road. That's A-M-Y-E-S. And that's in Mount Eden."},{"speaker":null,"text":"What day of the week would you like the property cleaned? — It doesn't really matter. Not Monday, but any other day. — 9We have a cleaner in your area later on Thursday, so shall we go for that day? We could have someone there by about 9.30 in the morning."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Do you charge an hourly rate or a total for the whole job? — We charge by the hour. It will work out to about $25 per hour. — I thought it might be closer to $30. And how long do you expect it to take? — 10Well, you said the house isn't large, so I'd guess no more than three hours at the most. We can occasionally finish a three-bedroom in two and a half, but that's probably not too realistic."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Section 2. You will hear a tour guide talking to visitors at a museum."},{"speaker":null,"text":"You probably won't have time to see everything today, so 11what I recommend you do is go to the Egyptian room first because it's everyone's favourite place and it gets very crowded with the school parties later in the day (A — eng mashhur eksponatlar avval). Oh, and I should mention that the photography gallery is undergoing refurbishment at the moment (C tuzoq — ta'mirda)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"It was designed by a local architect called William Craven in the 19th century, at a time when the city was developing rapidly with new factories. The museum's built in a very similar style to the railway station which was constructed at around the same time. 12That was designed by another architect, but William Craven did also provide the plans for the town hall (B) (factory va railway station — tuzoqlar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"The lovely big windows have been retained to let the daylight flood in, but 13the award-winning part of the project was the restoration of the area around the central hall — in particular, the beautiful wrought iron staircase (A). Unfortunately, the museum's original tiled floor had to be replaced (floor va windows — tuzoqlar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Since we don't charge admission fees, we had to find other ways of funding it. We did get some money from the Department of Culture at national level, but 14we had even more generous support from companies and industries here in the city who were our main benefactors (C — local business)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"So how will the museum mainly be spending its money in the next five years? We already work with schools and colleges. 15We consider the most important part of our work the restoration of the valuable historical objects… and this will continue to be where the most funding is allocated (A). Of course, it would be wonderful to purchase new objects, but we simply don't have the space (C — tuzoq)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"If you would like to learn more about our exhibits, 16I suggest you come to one of the Saturday morning lectures which are given every month by one of our team of experts (C). You can pick up leaflets too, but you'll only get a basic introduction from those; we're also working to update our website, but that's still at the planning stage (A va B — tuzoqlar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"17We're very well known for our collection of 18th-century paintings… Some of these are English landscapes and portraits, but we also have paintings by other European artists (C — turli mamlakatlar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"18The Farnley collection is a set of drawings by Paul Farnley. He was born in Ireland, but he came to work here in the city in the early 20th century and then made it his home (B — mahalliy rassom)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We have a display of kitchen appliances. 19There's an electric potato peeler from the 1970s which sold really well at the time, but no one's got one now (E — endi keng tarqalmagan narsalar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"You might also like to visit the fashion gallery. 20This is an exhibition which is running for the next few weeks only (D — vaqtinchalik ko'rgazma)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Section 3. You will hear two students, Frances and Sam, discussing business analysis tools with their tutor."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We liked the theory behind PEST analysis — political, economic, social and technological — 21although we're not sure if it was very applicable to our case. Some of the other groups had studies for which it worked really well and they said it was easy to use, but I felt it focused too much on the big picture and was unsuitable for our company (C) (E \"easy to use\" — boshqa guruhlar aytgan, tuzoq)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"On the other hand, I enjoyed using the drill down method. 22It was painstaking to do and we seemed to be working on it for ages, but the results were worth waiting for (D — juda ko'p vaqt oladi)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"I much preferred doing the PMI analysis. 23It was so straightforward… Fast and effective and it didn't make your brain hurt doing it. I agree, and you don't need any special training at all. Anyone can use it (E — ishlatish oson)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"The one tool that is critical to business, especially for larger companies, is Pareto analysis. By focusing on the critical 20% of their problems, they could generate 80% of the benefits. 24This would allow them to work faster and it also reduces their workload (A — vaqt va kuchni tejaydi)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"My favourite was the SWOT analysis — strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats — as it can be used in so many different situations. 25It works in large and small companies and even down to departmental level (G — deyarli barcha hajmdagi kompaniyalarga mos)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We initially looked at their strengths. The company, although it is small, is well known and has a very good reputation. The management are very committed to increasing the company profits. — 26Right, and the company has quite a lot of staff who have previously worked for distribution companies, so the knowledge is already there. That was something we didn't expect to find and is probably going to help them the most to achieve their goals (B — tajribali xodimlar)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"27I did think you missed something quite pertinent to their future growth… You didn't consider the potential for establishing an offshore division (B — chet elda ofis ochish). You talked about the company negotiating better terms with its suppliers (A — allaqachon ko'rib chiqilgan)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"So what did you think about the threats we identified? — 28I was really pleased to see that you considered how the government's planned environmental policy could really affect the viability of this venture. With this law being introduced next year… (C — yangi qonunchilik)"},{"speaker":null,"text":"So, Sam, what did you learn from this assignment? — 29It was great to study the different tools in books, but applying them in the real world was much harder than I thought (C — nazariya va amaliyot orasidagi farq)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"You've got the format correct with the necessary headings (B — tuzoq), and you've got sufficient details under the different headings (C — tuzoq). 30Just remember to state whether or not you think the company should go ahead with a new venture (A — yakuniy xulosa bering)."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Section 4. You will hear a student giving an overview of a research project — an employment survey on graduates."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We wanted to get some data on what happens to students after they graduate. 31We focused on graduates from the course in business management, since this is one of the most popular and long-established courses."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We decided to use two different data gathering methods. We started off by emailing a brief questionnaire to all last year's graduates, and then 32we selected a number of those who had replied, and with them we carried out phone interviews. We'd originally intended to use face-to-face interviews, but didn't feel that would be practical."},{"speaker":null,"text":"Our most surprising finding was 33just how many graduates had gone on to work towards an additional qualification, rather than getting a job immediately. That was 32 percent. Of the rest, a very small proportion were unemployed, just four percent. 34More than half of them were in the public sector, with a sizable minority in the private sector."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We were also interested in the attitudes of those who were employed towards their work. 35The majority said that their expectations had been fulfilled."},{"speaker":null,"text":"There were really three main skills which the graduates felt they'd gained. 36They highlighted the fact that they developed the ability to work as members of a team. Another skill was that of personal organization. 37And finally, a lot of them said that what they learned about approaches to problem solving had been very useful."},{"speaker":null,"text":"We also asked them about which elements of the course had been least valuable. 38To our surprise, the thing that was mentioned most often here was presentations. The reason given for this was that they felt they weren't trained how to do it properly. 39And the second thing that got very negative feedback was work on essay writing. Most people thought this was unnecessary."},{"speaker":null,"text":"And finally, 40some respondents said that they would have liked more guidance on the best way to go about looking for a job, that the course could have done more to help them."}],"markers":[{"question_ordinal":1,"time_seconds":30,"text":"I'm in the South West"},{"question_ordinal":2,"time_seconds":55,"text":"Well, one of the bedrooms is quite small, so it's probably really two double rooms"},{"question_ordinal":3,"time_seconds":62,"text":"We have the small bedroom set up as an office"},{"question_ordinal":4,"time_seconds":75,"text":"Then there's the lounge, and as well as that, we have a family room"},{"question_ordinal":5,"time_seconds":180,"text":"I'm not so worried about that, but I would like the sheets changed. — That's no problem. We can do that (A)"},{"question_ordinal":6,"time_seconds":205,"text":"It really needs doing more often than that. You can have it done every month if you like, but three months is what we usually recommend (B — the carpet)"},{"question_ordinal":7,"time_seconds":230,"text":"Well, it's no problem to put a load of washing in the machine. I can do that, but I would like to have the ironing done (B)"},{"question_ordinal":8,"time_seconds":260,"text":"Yes. It's 48 Ames Road. That's A-M-Y-E-S"},{"question_ordinal":9,"time_seconds":285,"text":"We have a cleaner in your area later on Thursday, so shall we go for that day?"},{"question_ordinal":10,"time_seconds":320,"text":"Well, you said the house isn't large, so I'd guess no more than three hours at the most"}]},"groups":[{"external_id":"listening:s1:g1","ordinal":1,"instructions":"Questions 1–4 Complete the form below. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer. HOMECARE CLEANING AGENCYHome Details","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q1","ordinal":1,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"Location: in the ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"southwest","accepted_variants":["south west","south-west"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":30,"text":"I'm in the South West"}},{"external_id":"listening:q2","ordinal":2,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"◦ two ____ bedrooms (third bedroom used as ____ )","options":null,"correct_answer":"double","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":55,"text":"Well, one of the bedrooms is quite small, so it's probably really two double rooms"}},{"external_id":"listening:q3","ordinal":3,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"(third bedroom used as ____ )","options":null,"correct_answer":"an office","accepted_variants":["office"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":62,"text":"We have the small bedroom set up as an office"}},{"external_id":"listening:q4","ordinal":4,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"◦ ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"lounge","accepted_variants":["a lounge"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":75,"text":"Then there's the lounge, and as well as that, we have a family room"}}]},{"external_id":"listening:s1:g2","ordinal":2,"instructions":"Questions 5–7 Choose the correct answer.","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q5","ordinal":5,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"5 Which extra service does the agency agree to provide?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"changing the bed linen"},{"label":"B","text":"washing the windows"},{"label":"C","text":"cleaning the fridge"}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":180,"text":"I'm not so worried about that, but I would like the sheets changed. — That's no problem. We can do that (A)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q6","ordinal":6,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"6 What will be cleaned more thoroughly every three months?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"the children's room"},{"label":"B","text":"the carpet"},{"label":"C","text":"the bathroom"}],"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":205,"text":"It really needs doing more often than that. You can have it done every month if you like, but three months is what we usually recommend (B — the carpet)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q7","ordinal":7,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"7 The woman would like the cleaners to","options":[{"label":"A","text":"do the washing"},{"label":"B","text":"iron the clothes"},{"label":"C","text":"put the clothes away"}],"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":230,"text":"Well, it's no problem to put a load of washing in the machine. I can do that, but I would like to have the ironing done (B)"}}]},{"external_id":"listening:s1:g3","ordinal":3,"instructions":"Questions 8–10 Complete the form below. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer. HOMECARE CLEANING AGENCYCustomer Details","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q8","ordinal":8,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"Address: 48 ____ Road, Mount Eden","options":null,"correct_answer":"amyes","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":260,"text":"Yes. It's 48 Ames Road. That's A-M-Y-E-S"}},{"external_id":"listening:q9","ordinal":9,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"Day of job: ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"thursday","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":285,"text":"We have a cleaner in your area later on Thursday, so shall we go for that day?"}},{"external_id":"listening:q10","ordinal":10,"type":"form_completion","prompt":"Maximum length of job: ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"3 hours","accepted_variants":["three hours","3"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":320,"text":"Well, you said the house isn't large, so I'd guess no more than three hours at the most"}}]}]},{"external_id":"listening:s2","kind":"listening","ordinal":2,"duration_seconds":510,"stimulus":{"type":"audio","audio_url":"audio/listening.mp3","transcript":[],"markers":[{"question_ordinal":11,"time_seconds":455,"text":"what I recommend you do is go to the Egyptian room first because it's everyone's favourite place and it gets very crowded with the school parties later in the day (A — eng mashhur eksponatlar avval)"},{"question_ordinal":12,"time_seconds":495,"text":"That was designed by another architect, but William Craven did also provide the plans for the town hall (B)"},{"question_ordinal":13,"time_seconds":530,"text":"the award-winning part of the project was the restoration of the area around the central hall — in particular, the beautiful wrought iron staircase (A)"},{"question_ordinal":14,"time_seconds":560,"text":"we had even more generous support from companies and industries here in the city who were our main benefactors (C — local business)"},{"question_ordinal":15,"time_seconds":595,"text":"We consider the most important part of our work the restoration of the valuable historical objects… and this will continue to be where the most funding is allocated (A)"},{"question_ordinal":16,"time_seconds":625,"text":"I suggest you come to one of the Saturday morning lectures which are given every month by one of our team of experts (C)"},{"question_ordinal":17,"time_seconds":700,"text":"We're very well known for our collection of 18th-century paintings… Some of these are English landscapes and portraits, but we also have paintings by other European artists (C — turli mamlakatlar)"},{"question_ordinal":18,"time_seconds":720,"text":"The Farnley collection is a set of drawings by Paul Farnley. He was born in Ireland, but he came to work here in the city in the early 20th century and then made it his home (B — mahalliy rassom)"},{"question_ordinal":19,"time_seconds":755,"text":"There's an electric potato peeler from the 1970s which sold really well at the time, but no one's got one now (E — endi keng tarqalmagan narsalar)"},{"question_ordinal":20,"time_seconds":780,"text":"This is an exhibition which is running for the next few weeks only (D — vaqtinchalik ko'rgazma)"}]},"groups":[{"external_id":"listening:s2:g1","ordinal":1,"instructions":"Questions 11–16 Choose the correct answer. Museum tour","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q11","ordinal":11,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"11 What does the tour guide advise the visitors to do in the museum today?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"see the most popular exhibits first"},{"label":"B","text":"pay a brief visit to each gallery"},{"label":"C","text":"go to the photography gallery last"}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":455,"text":"what I recommend you do is go to the Egyptian room first because it's everyone's favourite place and it gets very crowded with the school parties later in the day (A — eng mashhur eksponatlar avval)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q12","ordinal":12,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"12 The museum was designed by William Craven, who also designed","options":[{"label":"A","text":"a textile factory"},{"label":"B","text":"a town hall"},{"label":"C","text":"a railway station"}],"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":495,"text":"That was designed by another architect, but William Craven did also provide the plans for the town hall (B)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q13","ordinal":13,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"13 The museum won an award for the preservation of the","options":[{"label":"A","text":"staircase"},{"label":"B","text":"floor"},{"label":"C","text":"windows"}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":530,"text":"the award-winning part of the project was the restoration of the area around the central hall — in particular, the beautiful wrought iron staircase (A)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q14","ordinal":14,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"14 Most of the money for the project came from","options":[{"label":"A","text":"the public"},{"label":"B","text":"the government"},{"label":"C","text":"local business"}],"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":560,"text":"we had even more generous support from companies and industries here in the city who were our main benefactors (C — local business)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q15","ordinal":15,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"15 Over the next five years, the museum will invest mainly in","options":[{"label":"A","text":"restoring existing collections."},{"label":"B","text":"developing educational programmes."},{"label":"C","text":"purchasing new objects for display."}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":595,"text":"We consider the most important part of our work the restoration of the valuable historical objects… and this will continue to be where the most funding is allocated (A)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q16","ordinal":16,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"16 Visitors who are interested in learning more about the exhibits should","options":[{"label":"A","text":"visit the museum's website"},{"label":"B","text":"read the leaflet on display"},{"label":"C","text":"attend the monthly lecture"}],"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":625,"text":"I suggest you come to one of the Saturday morning lectures which are given every month by one of our team of experts (C)"}}]},{"external_id":"listening:s2:g2","ordinal":2,"instructions":"Questions 17–20 What information does the guide give about each of the following collections? Choose FOUR correct answers, A–F, next to questions 17–20.","shared_options":[{"label":"A","text":"has been shown in different museums"},{"label":"B","text":"consists of work by a local resident"},{"label":"C","text":"has exhibits from various countries"},{"label":"D","text":"is only on temporary display"},{"label":"E","text":"shows things that are no longer common"},{"label":"F","text":"is on loan from a foreign museum"}],"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q17","ordinal":17,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"17 18th-century paintings ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":700,"text":"We're very well known for our collection of 18th-century paintings… Some of these are English landscapes and portraits, but we also have paintings by other European artists (C — turli mamlakatlar)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q18","ordinal":18,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"18 Farnley collection ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":720,"text":"The Farnley collection is a set of drawings by Paul Farnley. He was born in Ireland, but he came to work here in the city in the early 20th century and then made it his home (B — mahalliy rassom)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q19","ordinal":19,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"19 Kitchen appliances ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"E","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":755,"text":"There's an electric potato peeler from the 1970s which sold really well at the time, but no one's got one now (E — endi keng tarqalmagan narsalar)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q20","ordinal":20,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"20 Fashion gallery ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"D","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":780,"text":"This is an exhibition which is running for the next few weeks only (D — vaqtinchalik ko'rgazma)"}}]}]},{"external_id":"listening:s3","kind":"listening","ordinal":3,"duration_seconds":510,"stimulus":{"type":"audio","audio_url":"audio/listening.mp3","transcript":[],"markers":[{"question_ordinal":21,"time_seconds":845,"text":"although we're not sure if it was very applicable to our case. Some of the other groups had studies for which it worked really well and they said it was easy to use, but I felt it focused too much on the big picture and was unsuitable for our company (C)"},{"question_ordinal":22,"time_seconds":870,"text":"It was painstaking to do and we seemed to be working on it for ages, but the results were worth waiting for (D — juda ko'p vaqt oladi)"},{"question_ordinal":23,"time_seconds":895,"text":"It was so straightforward… Fast and effective and it didn't make your brain hurt doing it. I agree, and you don't need any special training at all. Anyone can use it (E — ishlatish oson)"},{"question_ordinal":24,"time_seconds":930,"text":"This would allow them to work faster and it also reduces their workload (A — vaqt va kuchni tejaydi)"},{"question_ordinal":25,"time_seconds":955,"text":"It works in large and small companies and even down to departmental level (G — deyarli barcha hajmdagi kompaniyalarga mos)"},{"question_ordinal":26,"time_seconds":1035,"text":"Right, and the company has quite a lot of staff who have previously worked for distribution companies, so the knowledge is already there. That was something we didn't expect to find and is probably going to help them the most to achieve their goals (B — tajribali xodimlar)"},{"question_ordinal":27,"time_seconds":1060,"text":"I did think you missed something quite pertinent to their future growth… You didn't consider the potential for establishing an offshore division (B — chet elda ofis ochish)"},{"question_ordinal":28,"time_seconds":1095,"text":"I was really pleased to see that you considered how the government's planned environmental policy could really affect the viability of this venture. With this law being introduced next year… (C — yangi qonunchilik)"},{"question_ordinal":29,"time_seconds":1125,"text":"It was great to study the different tools in books, but applying them in the real world was much harder than I thought (C — nazariya va amaliyot orasidagi farq)"},{"question_ordinal":30,"time_seconds":1155,"text":"Just remember to state whether or not you think the company should go ahead with a new venture (A — yakuniy xulosa bering)"}]},"groups":[{"external_id":"listening:s3:g1","ordinal":1,"instructions":"Questions 21–25 What are the characteristics of the following analysis methods? Choose FIVE correct letters, A–G, next to questions 21–25.","shared_options":[{"label":"A","text":"it will save a lot of business time and effort"},{"label":"B","text":"it is visualized"},{"label":"C","text":"it does not fit our company"},{"label":"D","text":"it will take too long"},{"label":"E","text":"it is easy to use"},{"label":"F","text":"it is difficult to apply"},{"label":"G","text":"it is suitable to almost all sized companies"}],"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q21","ordinal":21,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"21 PEST ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":845,"text":"although we're not sure if it was very applicable to our case. Some of the other groups had studies for which it worked really well and they said it was easy to use, but I felt it focused too much on the big picture and was unsuitable for our company (C)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q22","ordinal":22,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"22 Drill Down ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"D","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":870,"text":"It was painstaking to do and we seemed to be working on it for ages, but the results were worth waiting for (D — juda ko'p vaqt oladi)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q23","ordinal":23,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"23 PMI ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"E","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":895,"text":"It was so straightforward… Fast and effective and it didn't make your brain hurt doing it. I agree, and you don't need any special training at all. Anyone can use it (E — ishlatish oson)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q24","ordinal":24,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"24 Pareto ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":930,"text":"This would allow them to work faster and it also reduces their workload (A — vaqt va kuchni tejaydi)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q25","ordinal":25,"type":"matching_information","prompt":"25 SWOT ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"G","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":955,"text":"It works in large and small companies and even down to departmental level (G — deyarli barcha hajmdagi kompaniyalarga mos)"}}]},{"external_id":"listening:s3:g2","ordinal":2,"instructions":"Questions 26–30 Choose the correct answer.","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q26","ordinal":26,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"26 What does Frances consider as the best strength of the company?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"reputation"},{"label":"B","text":"experienced employees"},{"label":"C","text":"management"}],"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1035,"text":"Right, and the company has quite a lot of staff who have previously worked for distribution companies, so the knowledge is already there. That was something we didn't expect to find and is probably going to help them the most to achieve their goals (B — tajribali xodimlar)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q27","ordinal":27,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"27 What factor did Sam overlook for the future growth of the company?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"seek for cheaper suppliers"},{"label":"B","text":"set up an overseas office"},{"label":"C","text":"compete with major competitors"}],"correct_answer":"B","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1060,"text":"I did think you missed something quite pertinent to their future growth… You didn't consider the potential for establishing an offshore division (B — chet elda ofis ochish)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q28","ordinal":28,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"28 Which of the following can be the threat to a company?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"increasing competition"},{"label":"B","text":"outdated technology"},{"label":"C","text":"new legislation"}],"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1095,"text":"I was really pleased to see that you considered how the government's planned environmental policy could really affect the viability of this venture. With this law being introduced next year… (C — yangi qonunchilik)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q29","ordinal":29,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"29 What has Sam learned from the research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"using better tools"},{"label":"B","text":"cost of a successful business"},{"label":"C","text":"gap between reality and theory"}],"correct_answer":"C","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1125,"text":"It was great to study the different tools in books, but applying them in the real world was much harder than I thought (C — nazariya va amaliyot orasidagi farq)"}},{"external_id":"listening:q30","ordinal":30,"type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"30 What is the professor's suggestion for the report?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"give a final determination"},{"label":"B","text":"reorganize a clear structure"},{"label":"C","text":"add more detailed information"}],"correct_answer":"A","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1155,"text":"Just remember to state whether or not you think the company should go ahead with a new venture (A — yakuniy xulosa bering)"}}]}]},{"external_id":"listening:s4","kind":"listening","ordinal":4,"duration_seconds":510,"stimulus":{"type":"audio","audio_url":"audio/listening.mp3","transcript":[],"markers":[{"question_ordinal":31,"time_seconds":1240,"text":"We focused on graduates from the course in business management, since this is one of the most popular and long-established courses"},{"question_ordinal":32,"time_seconds":1260,"text":"we selected a number of those who had replied, and with them we carried out phone interviews"},{"question_ordinal":33,"time_seconds":1285,"text":"just how many graduates had gone on to work towards an additional qualification, rather than getting a job immediately. That was 32 percent"},{"question_ordinal":34,"time_seconds":1305,"text":"More than half of them were in the public sector"},{"question_ordinal":35,"time_seconds":1315,"text":"The majority said that their expectations had been fulfilled"},{"question_ordinal":36,"time_seconds":1345,"text":"They highlighted the fact that they developed the ability to work as members of a team"},{"question_ordinal":37,"time_seconds":1365,"text":"And finally, a lot of them said that what they learned about approaches to problem solving had been very useful"},{"question_ordinal":38,"time_seconds":1380,"text":"To our surprise, the thing that was mentioned most often here was presentations"},{"question_ordinal":39,"time_seconds":1410,"text":"And the second thing that got very negative feedback was work on essay writing. Most people thought this was unnecessary"},{"question_ordinal":40,"time_seconds":1430,"text":"some respondents said that they would have liked more guidance on the best way to go about looking for a job, that the course could have done more to help them"}]},"groups":[{"external_id":"listening:s4:g1","ordinal":1,"instructions":"Questions 31–40 Complete the notes below. Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer. Employment Survey on Graduates","shared_options":null,"questions":[{"external_id":"listening:q31","ordinal":31,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ interviews from which subject: ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"business management","accepted_variants":["business"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1240,"text":"We focused on graduates from the course in business management, since this is one of the most popular and long-established courses"}},{"external_id":"listening:q32","ordinal":32,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ two research methods: email questionnaires and ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"phone interviews","accepted_variants":["phone interview","telephone interviews"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1260,"text":"we selected a number of those who had replied, and with them we carried out phone interviews"}},{"external_id":"listening:q33","ordinal":33,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ 32% of students tended to acquire another ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"qualification","accepted_variants":["qualifications"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1285,"text":"just how many graduates had gone on to work towards an additional qualification, rather than getting a job immediately. That was 32 percent"}},{"external_id":"listening:q34","ordinal":34,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ most of students work in the ____ sector","options":null,"correct_answer":"public","accepted_variants":[],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1305,"text":"More than half of them were in the public sector"}},{"external_id":"listening:q35","ordinal":35,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ majority are happy with: ____","options":null,"correct_answer":"expectations","accepted_variants":["expectation"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1315,"text":"The majority said that their expectations had been fulfilled"}},{"external_id":"listening:q36","ordinal":36,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ working as a ____ member","options":null,"correct_answer":"team","accepted_variants":["a team"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1345,"text":"They highlighted the fact that they developed the ability to work as members of a team"}},{"external_id":"listening:q37","ordinal":37,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ ____ ability","options":null,"correct_answer":"problem solving","accepted_variants":["problem-solving","problemsolving"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1365,"text":"And finally, a lot of them said that what they learned about approaches to problem solving had been very useful"}},{"external_id":"listening:q38","ordinal":38,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ ____ (lack of training)","options":null,"correct_answer":"presentations","accepted_variants":["presentation"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1380,"text":"To our surprise, the thing that was mentioned most often here was presentations"}},{"external_id":"listening:q39","ordinal":39,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ advice on ____ (unnecessary)","options":null,"correct_answer":"essay writing","accepted_variants":["essay-writing"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1410,"text":"And the second thing that got very negative feedback was work on essay writing. Most people thought this was unnecessary"}},{"external_id":"listening:q40","ordinal":40,"type":"note_completion","prompt":"◦ advice on finding a ____ (not enough)","options":null,"correct_answer":"job","accepted_variants":["a job"],"evidence":{"kind":"transcript","time_seconds":1430,"text":"some respondents said that they would have liked more guidance on the best way to go about looking for a job, that the course could have done more to help them"}}]}]}]}$seed$::jsonb);

